From b4ba1f0a9a63eabfd2f24ea4829864157e8704b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: melonDS Wi-Fi LAN <rickandmotyc137@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 20:26:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] LAN: make local multiplayer survive Wi-Fi and phone
 hotspots

- Disable ENet's packet throttle on every peer. It randomly discards
  unreliable packets whenever RTT rises, and all DS wireless frames are
  sent unreliable, so every Wi-Fi latency bump dropped MP frames. This
  alone took replies missed on a clean link from ~2.5% to 0.
- Adaptive receive wait: derive the reply deadline from measured
  CMD->reply exchange times (RFC 6298 style) and ENet RTT, clamped to
  [MinTimeout, MaxTimeout], with a decaying backoff after timeouts.
  The deadline now covers the whole exchange instead of each packet.
- Honour MPInterface::RecvTimeout (the "receive timeout" setting) as the
  lower bound; previously LAN mode ignored it and always used 25ms.
- Stale-packet window scales with the wait instead of a fixed 16ms.
- Optional redundant MP frames, sent only to peers that advertise
  duplicate filtering through a new Cmd_Caps (0x40) control command.
  Older versions ignore unknown commands, so the protocol stays
  compatible in both directions.
- Discovery beacons also go to each interface's broadcast address, so
  a device acting as a Wi-Fi hotspot can be found by its clients.
- Expose tuning (SetTuning) and live stats (GetStats).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
